2	//!
3	//! # ATX Headings (§4.2)
4	//!
5	//! An ATX heading consists of 1-6 `#` characters followed by a space and heading
6	//! text. The number of `#` characters determines the heading level.
7	//!
8	//! ```markdown
9	//! # Heading 1
10	//! ## Heading 2
11	//! ### Heading 3
12	//! ```
13	//!
14	//! # Setext Headings (§4.3)
15	//!
16	//! A setext heading consists of one or more lines of text followed by an
17	//! underline of `=` (level 1) or `-` (level 2) characters.
18	//!
19	//! ```markdown
20	//! Heading 1
21	//! =========
22	//!
23	//! Heading 2
24	//! ---------
25	//! ```
